        <p>UNDER DEED OF ASSIGNMENT,—TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION, on FRIDAY NExr, the Bth Day of July. 1893 at 2.3) p.m on the premises. Longford-st., Warrington. Mr. VIOAA:3 COWDIILL is favoured With instructions from the Trustees under a Deed of Assignment for the benent of Creditors, dated 16th of December, 1897,t0 sell the STOCK, PLANT and other effects of the business of a Mineral Water Manufacturer. carried on by Mr. James Wilkinson in Loneford-street. Warrington. The said:effe3ts comprise Soda Water Machine (by Galloway), Paragon Filter (by Bylands). Filling and Corking Machines (by Eagles), Gas Holder an 4 Generator, Bottle Washer and -Rinser with Brushing head, Syrup Apparatus, Brewing Apparatus, together with a large stoak of Boxes and Bottles. Also the DORSH and FLOAT, ,ta. N.B.—Mr. COWDBLL is authorised at any time before the date of Sale to receive offers to buy the Business as a going concern. If no offer is received the above property will be offered in such lots as the Auctioneer may decide on the spot.</p>
        <p>By order of the Trustee. THOMAS COWDELL, Auctioneer, Scotland-road, Warrington.</p>
